From 2f1110e6d450c83f4d4966a7d1b6dae85758f474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emergent E1 Agent <emergent-agent@darts-caller-ext.local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:31:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(listeners): eliminate P0 lifecycle leaks (Issue #9 P0-1 +
 P0-2)

P0-1 (next-player-on-take-out-stuck.ts):
- Remove the module-top-level monkey-patch of Document.prototype.addEventListener
  and the unbounded eventListenersMap. It leaked every document listener from
  Autodarts core / other scripts and was never rolled back on feature-remove.
- Replace with stable module-scope handler references (clickHandlerRef,
  fullscreenHandlerRef) that guard registration and are removed cleanly in
  nextPlayerOnTakeOutStuckOnRemove(). This also fixes P1-1 (broken cleanup
  via callback.name lookup returning the wrong handler on re-enable).

P0-2 (discord-webhooks.ts + lobby.content/index.ts):
- Track the Start-Game MutationObserver in a module-scope ref, add a guard so
  only one observer is ever attached to document.body, and disconnect it on
  feature remove.
- Add discordWebhooksOnRemove() that disconnects the observer, cancels the
  pending autoStartTimer, removes the injected Discord button and resets
  per-session state.
- Register discordWebhooksOnRemove() in lobby.content/index.ts route-leave
  branch, analogous to botSkinPickerOnRemove() etc.

No gameplay/UI/feature behaviour changes. P0-3 (caller.ts blob-cleanup
interval) and P1-2 (caller.ts unlockAudio listeners) intentionally deferred
per user request.
